{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | sed -n '515,565p;755,810p;1010,1075p'; nl -ba test/dao/space/query_test.cljc | sed -n '1120,1165p'; nl -ba docs/design/datom.world.md | head -90\"","aggregated_output":"   515\t                 ring/capacity-key (or capacity vm/default-stream-capacity)}))\n   516\t\n   517\t\n   518\t(defn make-vm\n   519\t  \"Construct the shell's evaluator on `yin.vm`.\n   520\t\n   521\t   The shell is the composition that chooses the VM's transport: the\n   522\t   evaluator is handed `:make-stream` bound to the ring buffer and the\n   523\t   `stream` module registered in its registry.  No telemetry stream is\n   524\t   installed, and the VM owns no program medium: `make-session` builds the\n   525\t   medium, its attachment, the observer, and the VM together.\n   526\t\n   527\t   `extra-primitives` is the host-supplied map merged over the REPL's own\n   528\t   primitives, so an embedding host's functions win a name collision.\n   529\t\n   530\t   `link-pair` is the link pair `(require ...)` lowers to\n   531\t   (yin.vm.linker.md section 6.1), held in the VM's private `:resources`\n   532\t   table; `make-session` composes one per VM, and the install children\n   533\t   the VM starts inherit it.\n   534\t\n   535\t   `query-pair` is the session's query call pair\n   536\t   (`yin.repl.query/make-pair`), supplied as the VM's FFI pair with its\n   537\t   call-out cursor; with it the registry carries the query bridge, so\n   538\t   `(require 'dao.space.query)` activates `dao.space.query/q`.\"\n   539\t  ([vm-type output-stream] (make-vm vm-type output-stream nil nil nil))\n   540\t  ([vm-type output-stream extra-primitives]\n   541\t   (make-vm vm-type output-stream extra-primitives nil nil))\n   542\t  ([vm-type output-stream extra-primitives link-pair]\n   543\t   (make-vm vm-type output-stream extra-primitives link-pair nil))\n   544\t  ([vm-type output-stream extra-primitives link-pair query-pair]\n   545\t   (when-not (contains? vm-constructors vm-type)\n   546\t     (throw (ex-info \"Unknown Yin REPL VM type\"\n   547\t                     {:vm-type vm-type\n   548\t                      :supported (vec (keys vm-constructors))})))\n   549\t   ((get vm-constructors vm-type)\n   550\t    (cond-> {:primitives (merge (make-repl-primitives output-stream)\n   551\t                                extra-primitives)\n   552\t             :modules (cond-> (module/register-stream-module\n   553\t                                (module/default-registry))\n   554\t                        query-pair query/register)\n   555\t             :make-stream make-ring-stream\n   556\t             ;; the task's capability secret (yin.vm.linker.md 7.3, r10):\n   557\t             ;; the REPL is the composition, so it mints one from its own\n   558\t             ;; random source, and a fresh one for every install child the\n   559\t             ;; task starts\n   560\t             :capability-secret (str (random-uuid))\n   561\t             :secret-source (fn [_origin] (str (random-uuid)))}\n   562\t      link-pair (assoc :link-request (:requests link-pair)\n   563\t                       :link-response (:responses link-pair))\n   564\t      query-pair (assoc :call-in (:call-in query-pair)\n   565\t                        :call-out (:call-out query-pair)\n   755\t\n   756\t\n   757\t;; =============================================================================\n   758\t;; Reading and classifying input\n   759\t;; =============================================================================\n   760\t\n   761\t(defn- read-forms\n   762\t  [input]\n   763\t  #?(:cljd (edn/read-string (str \"[\" input \"]\"))\n   764\t     :cljs (reader/read-string (str \"[\" input \"]\"))\n   765\t     :clj (clojure.core/read-string (str \"[\" input \"]\"))))\n   766\t\n   767\t\n   768\t(defn- command-form?\n   769\t  [form]\n   770\t  (and (seq? form)\n   771\t       (symbol? (first form))\n   772\t       (contains? command-heads (first form))))\n   773\t\n   774\t\n   775\t(defn- datom?\n   776\t  [value]\n   777\t  (and (vector? value) (= 5 (count value))))\n   778\t\n   779\t\n   780\t(defn- datom-stream?\n   781\t  [value]\n   782\t  (and (vector? value) (seq value) (every? datom? value)))\n   783\t\n   784\t\n   785\t(defn- ast-map?\n   786\t  [value]\n   787\t  (and (map? value) (keyword? (:type value))))\n   788\t\n   789\t\n   790\t(defn- bracket-balance\n   791\t  \"Open minus close brackets, ignoring string literals and `;` comments.\n   792\t   Positive means the input is incomplete.\"\n   793\t  [s]\n   794\t  (loop [chars (seq s)\n   795\t         depth 0\n   796\t         in-str? false]\n   797\t    (if (empty? chars)\n   798\t      depth\n   799\t      (let [ch (first chars)\n   800\t            tail (rest chars)]\n   801\t        (cond in-str? (cond (= ch \\\\) (recur (rest tail) depth true)\n   802\t                            (= ch \\\") (recur tail depth false)\n   803\t                            :else (recur tail depth true))\n   804\t              (= ch \\\") (recur tail depth true)\n   805\t              (= ch \\;) (recur (drop-while #(not= % \\newline) tail) depth false)\n   806\t              (#{\\( \\[ \\{} ch) (recur tail (inc depth) false)\n   807\t              (#{\\) \\] \\}} ch) (recur tail (dec depth) false)\n   808\t              :else (recur tail depth false))))))\n   809\t\n   810\t\n  1010\t   moves nothing ends the drive: a link whose content source cannot\n  1011\t   answer will not answer by waiting longer.  Returns\n  1012\t   `[state vm pending progress?]`, `pending` the links the interpreter\n  1013\t   reported `:pending`, and `progress?` true when a round moved\n  1014\t   something -- advanced a serve cursor, delivered a response or\n  1015\t   completed an install -- the fact the pending run's `:checks` resets\n  1016\t   on (yin.repl.link-policy.md section 3.1).  A refused or lost link\n  1017\t   raises as the VM's own, carrying the interrupted VM's minted\n  1018\t   identity.\n  1019\t\n  1020\t   A VM waiting on a `dao.space.query/q` call is driven the same way: the\n  1021\t   query interpreter (`yin.repl.query/serve`) answers from the session's\n  1022\t   indexer and the VM runs on.  Only a round the VM spends waiting on a\n  1023\t   link counts against `link-round-budget`; a query is answered in the\n  1024\t   round it is asked, so its rounds are bounded by `query-drive-budget`\n  1025\t   calls instead: a VM still waiting on a call once the drive has\n  1026\t   answered that many raises `query-call-limit-text` as its own error,\n  1027\t   the unanswered request abandoned with it.\"\n  1028\t  [state vm]\n  1029\t  (loop [i 0\n  1030\t         calls 0\n  1031\t         vm vm\n  1032\t         state state\n  1033\t         pending []\n  1034\t         progress? false]\n  1035\t    (let [link? (link-waiting? vm)\n  1036\t          query? (query/waiting? vm)]\n  1037\t      (cond\n  1038\t        (or (vm/halted? vm) (not (or link? query?)) (>= i link-round-budget))\n  1039\t        [state vm pending progress?]\n  1040\t\n  1041\t        (and query? (>= calls query-drive-budget))\n  1042\t        (throw (link-raise (ex-info query-call-limit-text\n  1043\t                                    {:reason :yin.repl.query/call-limit\n  1044\t                                     :limit query-drive-budget})\n  1045\t                           vm\n  1046\t                           (update state :query-pair query/abandon-requests)))\n  1047\t\n  1048\t        :else\n  1049\t        (let [served (when link?\n  1050\t                       (link/serve {:pair (:link-pair state)\n  1051\t                                    :source (:link-source state)}))\n  1052\t              answered (when query?\n  1053\t                         (query/serve {:pair (:query-pair state)\n  1054\t                                       :indexer (:indexer state)\n  1055\t                                       :limits {:row-limit query-row-limit\n  1056\t                                                :byte-limit query-byte-limit}\n  1057\t                                       :budget (min query-serve-budget\n  1058\t                                                    (- query-drive-budget\n  1059\t                                                       calls))}))\n  1060\t              state (cond-> state\n  1061\t                      served (assoc :link-pair (:pair served))\n  1062\t                      answered (assoc :query-pair (:pair answered)))\n  1063\t              pending (if (seq (:pending served)) (:pending served) pending)]\n  1064\t          (if (or (:progress? served) (:progress? answered))\n  1065\t            (let [vm' (try (vm/run vm)\n  1066\t                           (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error)\n  1067\t                                  error\n  1068\t                             (throw (link-raise error vm state))))]\n  1069\t              (recur (if link? (inc i) i)\n  1070\t                     (+ calls (:answered answered 0))\n  1071\t                     vm'\n  1072\t                     state\n  1073\t                     pending\n  1074\t                     true))\n  1075\t            [state vm pending progress?]))))))\n  1120\t        local (open-local source-datoms)\n  1121\t        intake (open-intake)\n  1122\t        store (jing-file/create-content-file path)]\n  1123\t    (try (let [{:keys [manifest-address]} (index/publish-index! local [intake])\n  1124\t               _ (loop [state (pool-state intake)]\n  1125\t                   (let [{:keys [signal state] :as r} (jing/observe-step! store\n  1126\t                                                                          state)]\n  1127\t                     (case signal\n  1128\t                       :dao.stream/ok (recur state)\n  1129\t                       (:dao.stream/blocked :dao.stream/end) nil\n  1130\t                       (throw (ex-info \"test observer hit a gap or defect\" r)))))\n  1131\t               coordinate (index/published-index {:dao.jing/type :dao.jing/file,\n  1132\t                                                  :path path}\n  1133\t                                                 manifest-address)\n  1134\t               transported (edn/read-string (pr-str coordinate))]\n  1135\t           (is (= coordinate transported) \"the coordinate is plain EDN\")\n  1136\t           (is (= {:dao.stream/type :dao.space.index/published,\n  1137\t                   :dao.stream/bound {:manifest-address manifest-address},\n  1138\t                   :dao.stream/comparator :dao.space.index/eavt,\n  1139\t                   :content-store {:dao.jing/type :dao.jing/file, :path path},\n  1140\t                   :manifest-address manifest-address}\n  1141\t                  transported)\n  1142\t               \"the complete exact coordinate map — an explicit finite bound\n  1143\t                carried as data, not a lifecycle flag\")\n  1144\t           (testing \"the coordinate survives a stream round-trip unchanged\"\n  1145\t             (let [carrier (ring-handle 4)]\n  1146\t               (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n  1147\t                      (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! carrier transported))))\n  1148\t               (let [r (stream/next carrier\n  1149\t                                    (:dao.stream/cursor\n  1150\t                                      (stream/cursor carrier\n  1151\t                                                     :dao.stream/oldest)))]\n  1152\t                 (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r)))\n  1153\t                 (is (= transported (:dao.stream/value r))))))\n  1154\t           (let [opened (query/open-published! transported)]\n  1155\t             (try (is (= (sort index/eavt-cmp source-datoms) (query/rows opened))\n  1156\t                      \"the transported coordinate opens and reads normally\")\n  1157\t                  (finally (query/close-published! opened)))))\n  1158\t         (finally (jing/close! store) (cleanup-file path)))))\n  1159\t\n  1160\t\n  1161\t(deftest failed-open-closes-the-store-it-opened\n  1162\t  (let [fx (publish-into-file [[1 :work/task \"Code\" 10 1]])]\n  1163\t    (try\n  1164\t      #?(:cljd\n  1165\t         (is true\n     1\t---\n     2\tdescription: Core philosophy, foundational axioms, invariants, primitives (tuples, streams, host boundaries), architectural commitments, design principles, code style, and development workflow for datom.world\n     3\t---\n     4\t\n     5\t# DATOM.WORLD ARCHITECTURAL FOUNDATIONS & DEVELOPMENT RULES\n     6\t\n     7\t## Core Philosophy\n     8\t\n     9\tEverything is data.\n    10\tInterpretation > abstraction.\n    11\tExplicit causality > implicit assumptions.\n    12\tRestrictions are a feature.\n    13\t\n    14\t### Foundational Axioms\n    15\t\n    16\t1. **Everything is a Stream**: All IO and data flow through append-only streams.\n    17\t2. **Interpretation Creates Semantics**: Data is syntax; semantics only emerge through interpretation (one truth, many perspectives).\n    18\t   At system scale, a \"system\" is an emergent property of interpreters of\n    19\t   pure data, not an object, service, or stored artifact. Find the\n    20\t   interpreters and the data they share to find the system.\n    21\t3. **Code and State are Datoms**: Code (Universal AST) and runtime execution state are structured datoms, enabling syntax independence and structural reflection.\n    22\t4. **Everything is a Continuation**: Computation is modeled as serializable, portable continuations that can pause, travel across streams, and resume anywhere.\n    23\t\n    24\t## Non-Negotiable Invariants\n    25\t\n    26\t- Do not introduce hidden global state.\n    27\t- Do not introduce implicit control flow.\n    28\t- Do not introduce callbacks; every callback is an event on a stream.\n    29\t- Do not introduce shared mutable state.\n    30\t- Do not collapse interpretation and execution into the same layer.\n    31\t- Do not assume graphs: graphs must be constructed explicitly from tuples.\n    32\t\n    33\t## Tuples and Datoms\n    34\t\n    35\tTuples are elements in an open moduli space, graded by dimension $n$. A tuple can be any dimension/size.\n    36\tA datom is the canonical persistent tuple `[e a v t m]` (entity, attribute, value, transaction, metadata). Persistent facts are immutable datoms.\n    37\tSource scope belongs to the interpreter, never to an appended tuple slot. Queries keep physical sources as separate db-values and express union or joins explicitly.\n    38\t\n    39\tSee [`docs/design/datom.md`](./datom.md) for full specification.\n    40\t\n    41\t## Streams\n    42\t\n    43\tAll IO is modeled as a stream. Functions consume streams and produce streams.\n    44\tNo direct function-to-function coupling without a stream boundary.\n    45\tSide effects must appear as stream emissions.\n    46\tStreams are values that can be sent through streams.\n    47\tStreams carry whatever values the consumer needs: no datom requirement, no privileged payload shape.\n    48\t\n    49\tA stream has no privileged reader, and its meaning is not in it. Any number\n    50\tof interpreters may observe the same medium, and each constructs its own\n    51\tsemantics from the same batches: a `yin.vm` evaluator observing a program\n    52\tstream constructs CESK state and executes it; `dao.space.index` observing\n    53\tthe very same stream materializes covered indexes, so `dao.space.query/q`\n    54\tanswers Datalog over the program as it grows. Neither knows the other\n    55\texists. The medium is their only coupling, and each observer's ignorance of\n    56\tthe other is load-bearing: the evaluator never consults an index to run,\n    57\tand the index never evaluates a form to index it. This is how axiom 2\n    58\tbecomes architecture: one stream, many interpretations, none of them\n    59\tthe stream's own.\n    60\t\n    61\tFunctions can take anything and return anything.\n    62\tAgents are functions, closures, or continuations in `yin.vm` that communicate with the outside world through `dao.stream`. Agent behavior is specified entirely through stream effects.\n    63\t\n    64\tSee [`docs/design/dao.stream.md`](./dao.stream.md) for full stream specification.\n    65\tSee [`docs/design/yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md`](./yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md) for VM architecture.\n    66\t\n    67\t### Host Boundaries\n    68\t\n    69\tA host boundary is a stream boundary, never a function call. The one\n    70\tsanctioned function-shaped contact is a `dao.stream` handle operation, whose\n    71\texhaustive outcome map is stream protocol, not an application callback.\n    72\t\n    73\t**Effects out.** Portable code appends an effect value describing what must\n    74\thappen. A host interpreter consumes that stream, performs the operation, and\n    75\tappends the outcome. Portable code reads the outcome. Correlation is by\n    76\tidentity in the data; neither side holds a reference to the other. A host with\n    77\tno implementation for an effect emits a qualified unsupported result. That is a\n    78\tcorrect outcome, not a gap to be filled.\n    79\t\n    80\t**Events in.** When the host initiates (a socket receives, a connection drops,\n    81\ta timer fires) the adapter appends one plain-data event and returns. It invokes\n    82\tnothing. An interpreter reads that stream and decides what the event means.\n    83\tConstructively: **a callback is replaced by a function that transforms an event\n    84\tto data on a stream.** The host's demand for a callback stops at that function.\n    85\t\n    86\t**Adapters.** An adapter is a map of those transform functions. That is all an\n    87\tadapter is. It is a value, not a namespace, and it is general: sockets, files,\n    88\ttimers and windows all deliver events by calling something, and an adapter is\n    89\twhat they call. Each entry takes the host's arguments and returns one value;\n    90\tthe append is the adapter's, not the entry's, so an entry cannot return a value\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc | sed -n '205,335p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc | sed -n '300,455p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc | sed -n '205,335p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc | sed -n '300,455p'\"","aggregated_output":"   205\t                :failure {:round round\n   206\t                          :root root\n   207\t                          :stage :transact\n   208\t                          :outcome (:dao.stream/outcome answer)})\n   209\t         false]))\n   210\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) e\n   211\t      [(assoc ix\n   212\t              :failure {:round round\n   213\t                        :stage :project\n   214\t                        :message (ex-message e)})\n   215\t       false])))\n   216\t\n   217\t\n   218\t(defn- materialize\n   219\t  \"Drain the intake into the store until it blocks.  Answers how many\n   220\t   payloads it materialized and, when the drain met a gap or a defect, what\n   221\t   it met.  The pool is not kept: its intake is dropped with the round.\"\n   222\t  [content-store pool]\n   223\t  (loop [pool pool\n   224\t         n 0]\n   225\t    (let [{:keys [signal], :as r} (jing/observe-step! content-store pool)]\n   226\t      (case signal\n   227\t        :dao.stream/ok (recur (:state r) (inc n))\n   228\t        :dao.stream/blocked [n nil]\n   229\t        [n signal]))))\n   230\t\n   231\t\n   232\t(defn- publish\n   233\t  \"Publish the covered indexes over every committed transaction through\n   234\t   the round's transactor, drain its intake into the store, and read the\n   235\t   manifest back from it.  Only a publication whose manifest the store\n   236\t   answers becomes the reported one, covering `:published` transactions.\"\n   237\t  [ix round]\n   238\t  (try\n   239\t    (let [{:keys [transactor pool]} (:publication ix)\n   240\t          {:keys [manifest-address]} (transactor/publish! transactor\n   241\t                                                          (:publish-opts ix))\n   242\t          [n defect] (materialize (:content-store ix) pool)]\n   243\t      (if defect\n   244\t        (assoc ix :failure {:round round :stage :materialize :outcome defect})\n   245\t        (do (index/read-manifest (:content-store ix) manifest-address)\n   246\t            (assoc ix\n   247\t                   :manifest-address manifest-address\n   248\t                   :published (:transactions ix)\n   249\t                   :published-payloads n))))\n   250\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) e\n   251\t      (assoc ix\n   252\t             :failure {:round round :stage :publish :message (ex-message e)}))))\n   253\t\n   254\t\n   255\t(defn- consume\n   256\t  \"Advance the observer past every packet still on the medium, handing each\n   257\t   to `f` with the indexer; a gap marks the indexer lost, after which no\n   258\t   packet reaches `f`.\"\n   259\t  [indexer f]\n   260\t  (loop [ix indexer]\n   261\t    (let [{:keys [status batch] observer' :observer}\n   262\t          (observer/observe-next (:observer ix))\n   263\t          ix (assoc ix :observer observer')]\n   264\t      (case status\n   265\t        :ok (recur (if (:lost? ix) ix (f ix batch)))\n   266\t        :gap (recur (assoc ix :lost? true))\n   267\t        ix))))\n   268\t\n   269\t\n   270\t(defn step\n   271\t  \"The round's index step: observe every packet `program-out` still holds\n   272\t   for this observer, commit each through the round's publication, publish\n   273\t   when any was committed, then drop the publication — its transactor,\n   274\t   intake, and pool — so the indexer carries none of this round's payloads\n   275\t   into the next.  A gap is recovered across, counted on the observer's\n   276\t   `:ingress-gaps`, and marks the indexer lost: the missing packet and\n   277\t   every later one are never called indexed.\"\n   278\t  [indexer round]\n   279\t  (let [ix (consume indexer\n   280\t                    (fn [ix packet]\n   281\t                      (first (commit (open-publication ix) packet round))))]\n   282\t    (dissoc (if (> (:transactions ix) (:transactions indexer))\n   283\t              (publish ix round)\n   284\t              ix)\n   285\t            :publication)))\n   286\t\n   287\t\n   288\t(defn skip\n   289\t  \"Advance the observer past every packet still on the medium without\n   290\t   indexing it: a round that threw before its program ran executes nothing,\n   291\t   so nothing is indexed.  A gap still marks the indexer lost.\"\n   292\t  [indexer]\n   293\t  (consume indexer (fn [ix _packet] ix)))\n   294\t\n   295\t\n   296\t(defn status\n   297\t  \"The indexer's state as the shell reports it.  It depends on the programs\n   298\t   evaluated, never on which evaluator ran them or on the shell's token,\n   299\t   so every VM reports the same status for the same inputs.\"\n   300\t  [indexer]\n   301\t  {:transactions (:transactions indexer)\n   302\t   :published? (and (some? (:manifest-address indexer))\n   303\t                    (= (:published indexer) (:transactions indexer)))\n   304\t   :lost? (:lost? indexer)\n   305\t   :gaps (:ingress-gaps (:observer indexer) 0)\n   306\t   :failure (:failure indexer)})\n   307\t\n   308\t\n   309\t(defn notice\n   310\t  \"What the round from `before` to `after` must tell the user, or nil: a\n   311\t   lost indexer (the round's code was not indexed), or a new failure (the\n   312\t   round's code was not committed or its publication is not readable).\n   313\t   A failure's `:stage` is `:project`, `:transact`, `:materialize` or\n   314\t   `:publish`.\"\n   315\t  [before after]\n   316\t  (let [{:keys [stage outcome message]} (:failure after)]\n   317\t    (cond\n   318\t      (:lost? after)\n   319\t      (str \"Warning: the code index lost a program batch; this round's code\"\n   320\t           \" was not indexed, and indexing is suspended until (reset)\")\n   321\t\n   322\t      (not= (:failure before) (:failure after))\n   323\t      (str \"Warning: this round's code is not in the published code index (\"\n   324\t           (name stage) \" failed\"\n   325\t           (when-let [detail (or message (some-> outcome name))]\n   326\t             (str \": \" detail))\n   327\t           \")\"))))\n   300\t  \"The canonical CBOR size of `x`, or nil when `x` is not portable data.\"\n   301\t  [x]\n   302\t  (try\n   303\t    (byte-length (cbor/encode x))\n   304\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) _ nil)))\n   305\t\n   306\t\n   307\t(defn- in-patterns\n   308\t  \"The patterns `query` declares under `:in`, nil when it declares none.\"\n   309\t  [query]\n   310\t  (if (map? query)\n   311\t    (some-> (:in query) vec)\n   312\t    (let [[marker & after] (drop-while #(not= :in %) query)]\n   313\t      (when marker (vec (take-while (complement keyword?) after))))))\n   314\t\n   315\t\n   316\t(defn- caller-patterns\n   317\t  \"The `:in` patterns the caller's inputs fill: every declared pattern but\n   318\t   the implicit index `$`.\"\n   319\t  [query]\n   320\t  (vec (remove #{'$} (in-patterns query))))\n   321\t\n   322\t\n   323\t(defn- split-args\n   324\t  \"`[inputs options]` of the arguments after the query: one input per\n   325\t   pattern of `caller-patterns`, a map among them included, then at most\n   326\t   one options map.  A refusal when the arguments do not fit.\"\n   327\t  [query args]\n   328\t  (let [n (count (caller-patterns query))\n   329\t        [inputs more] (split-at n args)]\n   330\t    (if (and (= n (count inputs))\n   331\t             (or (empty? more) (and (= 1 (count more)) (map? (first more)))))\n   332\t      [(vec inputs) (first more)]\n   333\t      (refusal ::query-failed\n   334\t               (str \"query failed: query input arity must match :in, \" n\n   335\t                    \" :in inputs and an optional options map expected, got \"\n   336\t                    (count args) \" arguments\")\n   337\t               nil))))\n   338\t\n   339\t\n   340\t(defn- with-index\n   341\t  \"`query` with the index bound to `$`, the first database input it names.\n   342\t   The index is implicit: a query's `:in` names only the caller's inputs,\n   343\t   with or without `$` among them, and those inputs fill the other\n   344\t   patterns in order.  A query without `:in` takes none.\"\n   345\t  [query]\n   346\t  (let [declared (in-patterns query)\n   347\t        in (into ['$] (caller-patterns query))]\n   348\t    (cond (nil? declared) query\n   349\t          (map? query) (assoc query :in in)\n   350\t          :else (let [[before [_ & after]] (split-with #(not= :in %) query)]\n   351\t                  (-> (vec before)\n   352\t                      (conj :in)\n   353\t                      (into in)\n   354\t                      (into (drop-while (complement keyword?) after)))))))\n   355\t\n   356\t\n   357\t(defn- view-of\n   358\t  \"The view the options name, or a refusal.\"\n   359\t  [options]\n   360\t  (cond\n   361\t    (nil? options) (:current views)\n   362\t\n   363\t    (not= #{:view} (set (keys options)))\n   364\t    (invalid (str \"q options must be {:view :current} or {:view :history}, got \"\n   365\t                  (pr-str options)))\n   366\t\n   367\t    (contains? views (:view options)) (get views (:view options))\n   368\t\n   369\t    :else (invalid (str \"q :view must be :current or :history, got \"\n   370\t                        (pr-str (:view options))))))\n   371\t\n   372\t\n   373\t(defn- row-count\n   374\t  \"Rows of a collected result: a relation or collection counts its\n   375\t   members, a scalar or tuple is one.\"\n   376\t  [result]\n   377\t  (if (or (set? result) (sequential? result) (nil? result))\n   378\t    (count result)\n   379\t    1))\n   380\t\n   381\t\n   382\t(defn- evaluate\n   383\t  [db view query inputs {:keys [row-limit byte-limit]}]\n   384\t  (let [result (try\n   385\t                 {:value (query/collect\n   386\t                           (apply query/q query (view db) inputs))}\n   387\t                 (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n   388\t                   {:refusal (refusal ::query-failed\n   389\t                                      (str \"query failed: \"\n   390\t                                           (or (ex-message e) (str e)))\n   391\t                                      nil)}))]\n   392\t    (if-let [r (:refusal result)]\n   393\t      r\n   394\t      (let [value (:value result)\n   395\t            rows (row-count value)\n   396\t            size (when (<= rows row-limit) (encoded-size value))]\n   397\t        (cond\n   398\t          (> rows row-limit)\n   399\t          (refusal ::result-limit\n   400\t                   (str \"the query result has \" rows\n   401\t                        \" rows, over the limit of \" row-limit)\n   402\t                   {::limit {:rows row-limit}})\n   403\t\n   404\t          (nil? size)\n   405\t          (refusal ::query-failed\n   406\t                   \"the query result is not portable Yin data\"\n   407\t                   nil)\n   408\t\n   409\t          (> size byte-limit)\n   410\t          (refusal ::result-limit\n   411\t                   (str \"the query result encodes to \" size\n   412\t                        \" bytes, over the limit of \" byte-limit)\n   413\t                   {::limit {:bytes byte-limit}})\n   414\t\n   415\t          :else {:ok value})))))\n   416\t\n   417\t\n   418\t(defn answer\n   419\t  \"The response to one call-pair `request`, answered from `indexer`\n   420\t   under `limits` (`{:row-limit n :byte-limit n}`).\"\n   421\t  [indexer limits request]\n   422\t  (let [id (apply2/request-id request)\n   423\t        [query & more] (apply2/request-args request)\n   424\t        answer (cond\n   425\t                 (not= op (apply2/request-op request))\n   426\t                 (refusal :dao.stream.apply/unknown-operation\n   427\t                          \"No handler for operation\"\n   428\t                          nil)\n   429\t\n   430\t                 (nil? (encoded-size (apply2/request-args request)))\n   431\t                 (invalid (str \"q takes portable Yin data only: nil, booleans,\"\n   432\t                               \" numbers, strings, keywords, symbols, and\"\n   433\t                               \" vectors, lists, sets and maps of them\"))\n   434\t\n   435\t                 (not (or (vector? query) (map? query)))\n   436\t                 (invalid (str \"q expects a query vector or map, got \"\n   437\t                               (pr-str query)))\n   438\t\n   439\t                 :else\n   440\t                 (let [split (split-args query more)\n   441\t                       [inputs options] (when-not (refused? split) split)\n   442\t                       view (when-not (refused? split) (view-of options))\n   443\t                       db (when-not (or (refused? split) (refused? view))\n   444\t                            (snapshot indexer))]\n   445\t                   (cond\n   446\t                     (refused? split) split\n   447\t                     (refused? view) view\n   448\t                     (refused? db) db\n   449\t                     :else (evaluate db view (with-index query) inputs\n   450\t                                     limits))))]\n   451\t    (if (refused? answer)\n   452\t      {apply2/id-key id, apply2/error-key answer}\n   453\t      (apply2/success-response id (:ok answer)))))\n   454\t\n   455\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
