{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | sed -n '635,685p;890,930p;1325,1360p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc | sed -n '1580,1675p'\"","aggregated_output":"   635\t   Reset and VM selection call this, so the whole composition is rebuilt as\n   636\t   one and each attachment capability is bound exactly once per medium\n   637\t   lifetime.\n   638\t\n   639\t   Both evaluators sit behind the same two stages (yin.vm.macro.md §10.1):\n   640\t   the expander observes `program-in` — `:program-stream`, watched by\n   641\t   `:observer` — and appends each expanded tree packet to `program-out` —\n   642\t   `:row-stream`, watched independently by the evaluator's `:row-observer`,\n   643\t   which loads each packet and runs it.  The code indexer's observer\n   644\t   (`yin.repl.index`) is a peer attached to `program-out` beside it; the\n   645\t   round advances each, and neither calls the other.  It records\n   646\t   `shell-token` as provenance and publishes into `index-store`.\n   647\t\n   648\t   The link pair is the session's (`yin.repl.link/make-pair`): the VM's\n   649\t   half lives in its private `:resources`, the interpreter's half beside\n   650\t   it under `:link-pair`.  The content pair and the name environment the\n   651\t   interpreter serves from are the shell's (`:link-source`), and outlive\n   652\t   a session rebuild.\n   653\t\n   654\t   The query call pair is the session's too (`yin.repl.query/make-pair`):\n   655\t   the VM's half is its FFI pair, the interpreter's half with its request\n   656\t   cursor sits under `:query-pair`, and the interpreter answers from the\n   657\t   session's `:indexer` as it stands when it serves.\"\n   658\t  [vm-type output-stream extra-primitives shell-token index-store]\n   659\t  (let [pair (link/make-pair)\n   660\t        query-pair (query/make-pair query-pair-capacity)\n   661\t        vm (make-vm vm-type output-stream extra-primitives pair query-pair)\n   662\t        program-in (make-attachment ingress-capacity)\n   663\t        program-out (make-attachment ingress-capacity)]\n   664\t    {:vm vm\n   665\t     :load-program (get program-loaders vm-type)\n   666\t     :program-stream (:stream program-in)\n   667\t     :program-identity (:identity program-in)\n   668\t     :observer (:observer program-in)\n   669\t     :expander (make-expander (:identity program-in) (:stream program-out))\n   670\t     :row-stream (:stream program-out)\n   671\t     :row-observer (:observer program-out)\n   672\t     :indexer (index/make-indexer {:observer ((:attach program-out))\n   673\t                                   :session-token shell-token\n   674\t                                   :content-store index-store})\n   675\t     :link-pair pair\n   676\t     :query-pair (dissoc query-pair :out-cursor)}))\n   677\t\n   678\t\n   679\t(defn- checked-link-policy\n   680\t  \"Validate the `:link-policy` creation option, failing closed at\n   681\t   assembly (yin.repl.link-policy.md section 3): `:manual` is the\n   682\t   default and today's behavior, a function `(fn [view])` is the\n   683\t   embedder's rule, and `:lease` is reserved for the phase-2 deadline --\n   684\t   refused, not implemented yet.  Anything else is refused with the\n   685\t   supported values named.\"\n   890\t   remains is the failed batch alone.  The VM is the one the round began\n   891\t   with, so a half-run continuation cannot be resumed — and its error\n   892\t   replayed — by the next input.  Output the round already emitted is\n   893\t   drained here, once.\"\n   894\t  [state error]\n   895\t  (let [carried (get-in (ex-data error) [:session :observer])\n   896\t        resume (fn [observer]\n   897\t                 (if (and observer\n   898\t                          carried\n   899\t                          (= (:stream carried) (:stream observer)))\n   900\t                   carried\n   901\t                   observer))\n   902\t        drained (assoc state\n   903\t                       :observer (drain-observer (resume (:observer state)))\n   904\t                       :row-observer (drain-observer\n   905\t                                       (resume (:row-observer state)))\n   906\t                       :indexer (index/skip (:indexer state)))\n   907\t        [state' output-text]\n   908\t        (drain-output\n   909\t          (cond-> drained\n   910\t            (> (ingress-gaps drained) (ingress-gaps state))\n   911\t            (assoc :ingress-loss? true)))]\n   912\t    [state' (str output-text (format-error error))]))\n   913\t\n   914\t\n   915\t(defn- run-index-stage\n   916\t  \"Drive the code indexer's observer over `program-out`: it commits each\n   917\t   forwarded packet as one transaction and publishes the covered indexes.\n   918\t   It runs before the evaluator, so a program is indexed whether its VM\n   919\t   returns, parks, or raises; the two observers meet only at the medium.\"\n   920\t  [state]\n   921\t  (update state :indexer index/step (:round state)))\n   922\t\n   923\t\n   924\t(defn- with-index-notice\n   925\t  \"Append what the round's index step lost, if anything, to its result\n   926\t   text; the evaluation's own answer is unchanged.\"\n   927\t  [[state text] notice]\n   928\t  (if notice\n   929\t    [state (if (str/blank? text) notice (str text \"\\n\" notice))]\n   930\t    [state text]))\n  1325\t          batch (encoder/program-batch program)\n  1326\t          append (stream/append! (:program-stream state') batch)]\n  1327\t      (if-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome append))\n  1328\t        [state (str \"Error: program batch not ingested: \"\n  1329\t                    (name (:dao.stream/outcome append)))]\n  1330\t        (let [expanded (try\n  1331\t                         (run-expander-stage state')\n  1332\t                         (catch #?(:cljd Object\n  1333\t                                   :clj Exception\n  1334\t                                   :cljs js/Error) error\n  1335\t                           {:failed (consume-failed-round state error)}))]\n  1336\t          (if-let [failed (:failed expanded)]\n  1337\t            failed\n  1338\t            (let [[expanded {:keys [errors forwarded]}] expanded\n  1339\t                  indexed (cond-> expanded\n  1340\t                            (pos? forwarded) run-index-stage)]\n  1341\t              (with-index-notice\n  1342\t                (cond\n  1343\t                  (> (ingress-gaps indexed) (ingress-gaps state'))\n  1344\t                  [(assoc indexed :ingress-loss? true)\n  1345\t                   (str \"Error: \" ingress-loss-text)]\n  1346\t\n  1347\t                  (pos? forwarded) (run-evaluation state indexed)\n  1348\t\n  1349\t                  :else [(assoc indexed :vm (:vm state))\n  1350\t                         (format-expansion-errors errors)])\n  1351\t                (when (pos? forwarded)\n  1352\t                  (index/notice (:indexer expanded)\n  1353\t                                (:indexer indexed)))))))))))\n  1354\t\n  1355\t\n  1356\t(defn- compile-clojure-forms\n  1357\t  [forms]\n  1358\t  (if (= 1 (count forms))\n  1359\t    (yang.clojure/compile (first forms))\n  1360\t    (yang.clojure/compile-program forms)))\n  1580\t;; The occurrence relation and root-scoped occurrence rules\n  1581\t;; =============================================================================\n  1582\t;; §6.1/§4.5: the structural half of the AST indexer — not yet an observer.\n  1583\t\n  1584\t(defn- occurrence-child-places\n  1585\t  \"`[[path-step child-id] …]` for every `node`/`nodes` slot of a row, in slot\n  1586\t   order. A `:node` slot's step is its row position (id 0, tag 1, first slot\n  1587\t   2 — the base of §2.5's own `[2 [3 0]]` example), a `:nodes` slot's step\n  1588\t   is the pair `[position i]`. Note `validate-rows`' defect paths number\n  1589\t   the first slot 1; §2.5's example is normative here.\"\n  1590\t  [row]\n  1591\t  (let [slots (get semantic-bytecode-grammar (semantic-bytecode-row-tag row))]\n  1592\t    (mapcat (fn [j [_ kind] v]\n  1593\t              (let [pos (+ j 2)]\n  1594\t                (case kind\n  1595\t                  :node (when v [[pos v]])\n  1596\t                  :nodes (map-indexed (fn [i cid] [[pos i] cid]) v)\n  1597\t                  nil)))\n  1598\t            (range (count slots)) slots (drop 2 row))))\n  1599\t\n  1600\t\n  1601\t(defn occurrences\n  1602\t  \"§6.1: the occurrence relation of a projected row set — one\n  1603\t   `[root path node]` tuple per place, so a structurally shared subtree\n  1604\t   (§4.4) yields one tuple per place and one node id. Computed by the same\n  1605\t   walk as the projection, so it is generic over every §2.3 tag. It is a\n  1606\t   pure function of the tree and carries no origin; a query fixes origin\n  1607\t   from the composition's side and joins on `[root path]` (§6.1). Assumes\n  1608\t   the walk terminates: projected ids are content addresses of their\n  1609\t   children, so a projected set is acyclic by construction (§4.1).\"\n  1610\t  [{:keys [root rows]}]\n  1611\t  (loop [frontier [[[] root]]\n  1612\t         tuples []]\n  1613\t    (if (empty? frontier)\n  1614\t      (set tuples)\n  1615\t      (let [children (mapcat (fn [[path id]]\n  1616\t                               (let [row (get rows id)]\n  1617\t                                 (map (fn [[step cid]] [(conj path step) cid])\n  1618\t                                      (when row (occurrence-child-places row)))))\n  1619\t                             frontier)]\n  1620\t        (recur children\n  1621\t               (into tuples (map (fn [[path id]] [root path id]) frontier)))))))\n  1622\t\n  1623\t\n  1624\t(def occurrence-rules\n  1625\t  \"§4.5/§7.7: root-scoped occurrence rules. `?root` is threaded through\n  1626\t   every head (`p-up`/`occ-anc`/`occ-bound?`) and the `[$occ …]` join is\n  1627\t   constrained to one root, so a binder in another tree of the same\n  1628\t   relation can never classify this tree's occurrence — the gap §4.5 names\n  1629\t   in an unscoped rule set. The ancestor walk is over path prefixes\n  1630\t   (`path-pop`), not row edges, so it is generic over every §2.3 tag. `$`\n  1631\t   must be the row relation and `$occ` the occurrence relation; the rules\n  1632\t   need `member?` and `path-pop` under `:fns` — see `occurrence-fns`.\n  1633\t   `?root` must be bound at every call: the bodies never bind it, and an\n  1634\t   unscoped invocation fails loudly rather than enumerate.\"\n  1635\t  '[[(p-up ?root ?child ?parent) [(path-pop ?child) ?parent]]\n  1636\t    [(occ-anc ?root ?a ?d) (p-up ?root ?d ?a)]\n  1637\t    [(occ-anc ?root ?a ?d) (p-up ?root ?d ?m) (occ-anc ?root ?a ?m)]\n  1638\t    [(occ-bound? ?root ?path ?name)\n  1639\t     (occ-anc ?root ?lam-path ?path)\n  1640\t     [$occ ?root ?lam-path ?lam]\n  1641\t     [?lam :lambda ?params _]\n  1642\t     [(member? ?params ?name)]]])\n  1643\t\n  1644\t\n  1645\t(def occurrence-fns\n  1646\t  \"The `:fns` map `occurrence-rules` requires (§6.3: quoted-symbol keys):\n  1647\t   membership over a `:syms`/`:nodes` vector, and one step up a §2.5 path\n  1648\t   (nil at the root, where no occurrence tuple carries the answer anyway).\"\n  1649\t  {'member? (fn [coll x] (boolean (some #(= % x) coll))),\n  1650\t   'path-pop (fn [p] (when (pos? (count p)) (subvec p 0 (dec (count p)))))})\n  1651\t\n  1652\t\n  1653\t(defn free-names\n  1654\t  \"§7.7 free-name extraction as a function: every `:variable` name free at\n  1655\t   some occurrence of `root`'s tree. `db` is the row relation\n  1656\t   (`query/relation` over the rows) and `occ` the occurrence relation\n  1657\t   (`occurrences`); both may hold several trees unioned (§6.1) — the rules\n  1658\t   are root-scoped, so only `root`'s binder classifies `root`'s\n  1659\t   occurrences. Conservative by construction: a name whose row is bound at\n  1660\t   one occurrence and free at another is included, never silently dropped\n  1661\t   (S7.6.1). The definition operator is syntax, never a name\n  1662\t   (Rule R), so it is never free.\"\n  1663\t  [db occ root]\n  1664\t  (disj (set (map first\n  1665\t                  (query/collect\n  1666\t                    (query/q '[:find ?name :in $ $occ % ?root\n  1667\t                               :where\n  1668\t                               [$occ ?root ?path ?v]\n  1669\t                               [?v :variable ?name]\n  1670\t                               (not (occ-bound? ?root ?path ?name))]\n  1671\t                             db occ occurrence-rules root\n  1672\t                             {:fns occurrence-fns}))))\n  1673\t        definition-operator))\n  1674\t\n  1675\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
